{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582799730,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffep6y7sQ71Rop5Va","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5785ffb001iipLgUn3SQrCdl","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffep6y7sQ71Rop5Va","messageID":"msg_1d5783b04001UeOAWgbUX0fEoA","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a13cb7bcc1db3aef","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md, lines 1-153\n1: ---\n2: name: sk-doc\n3: description: \"Documentation & component authoring hub: skills, agents, commands, READMEs, catalogs, playbooks, changelogs, goals, frontmatter.\"\n4: allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n5: version: 2.9.13.0\n6: metadata:\n7:   family: sk-util\n8: ---\n9: \n10: <!-- Keywords: sk-doc, documentation, markdown, authoring, parent-hub, mode-registry, hub-router, workflowmode, packetkind, sk-create-skill, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, sk-create-quality-control, human-voice-rules, hvr, shared-backbone, create-quality-control-pipeline -->\n11: \n12: # Documentation Authoring Hub (sk-doc)\n13: \n14: One advisor identity, fifteen workflow modes across fourteen packets, one shared sk-create-quality-control backbone.\n15: `sk-doc` is the parent hub for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring.\n16: It holds NO per-packet logic: it routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each packet keeps its own contract in its nested folder.\n17: The cross-cutting sk-create-quality-control pipeline (validators, global standards, frontmatter/llms/template assets) lives once in `shared/` and is consumed by every packet.\n18: \n19: **Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`; `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value, so every hub-root JSON routing file states the same release; `ROUTER.md` keeps its own document version.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n24: \n25: Use this skill for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring, and for document-quality work. The hub classifies the request, resolves a `workflowMode`, and loads the matching nested packet.\n26: \n27: | Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command |\n28: |------|------------|--------|---------|\n29: | **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n30: | **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder README, general or code-folder | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n31: | **sk-create-agent** | Scaffold an OpenCode agent (permission/authority frontmatter) | `sk-create-agent/` | `/create:agent` |\n32: | **sk-create-command** | Scaffold an OpenCode slash command (argument-hint + allowed-tools + router/presentation split) | `sk-create-command/` | `/create:command` |\n33: | **sk-create-feature-catalog** | Author a feature-catalog inventory package | `sk-create-feature-catalog/` | `/create:feature-catalog` |\n34: | **sk-create-manual-testing-playbook** | Author a manual-testing-playbook package | `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/` | `/create:manual-testing-playbook` |\n35: | **sk-create-benchmark** | Author MCP-promotion and behavior packages or inputs | `sk-create-benchmark/` | `/create:benchmark` |\n36: | **sk-create-changelog** | Author a global component changelog entry (version bump + topology-aware placement). Packet-local changelogs are deprecated | `sk-create-changelog/` | `/create:changelog` |\n37: | **sk-create-diff** | Produce a local, Git-free before/after review of an edited document (text/Markdown/HTML/DOCX/text-PDF) as a self-contained HTML report | `sk-create-diff/` | `/create:diff` |\n38: | **sk-create-repo-rule** | Create, revise or retire a repo-local rule under `repo-rules/` and wire it into `REPO RULES.md` (four decision tests refuse most requests) | `sk-create-repo-rule/` | `/create:repo-rule` |\n39: | **sk-create-with-human-voice** | Apply the Human Voice Rules to prose, or score prose against them, with a scope gate and a re-scan | `sk-create-with-human-voice/` | `/create:with-human-voice` |\n40: | **sk-create-frontmatter** | Own the YAML frontmatter contract: per-class field rules, the description budget, and the 4-part `version` derivation | `sk-create-frontmatter/` | — (routes via aliases) |\n41: | **sk-create-goal** | Author or revise a packet `goal.md`: the durable directive, three to seven self-contained completion criteria, and the phase-parent binding table (session-goal setting stays with the goal hooks) | `sk-create-goal/` | `/create:goal` |\n42: | **sk-create-quality-control** | Validate / score / optimize an EXISTING document (extract → DQI → HVR → validate) | `sk-create-quality-control/` | (routes via aliases) |\n43: \n44: ### When NOT to Use\n45: - Code implementation, tests, or debugging — use `sk-code`.\n46: - Git worktree, branch, commit, PR, or release work — use `sk-git`.\n47: - Spec-folder workflow / memory / save context — use `system-spec-kit`.\n48: - A measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source) — use `sk-design-md-generator`.\n49: - The `shared/` backbone is consumed by the packets, not invoked as a user workflow.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n54: \n55: Routing is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\n56: Stage 1 (hub → mode) selects a mode: `hub-router.json` `vocabularyClasses` is the one authored routing vocabulary.\n57: The `mode-registry.json` aliases, each packet's `Keyword triggers:` line and the root `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against it.\n58: `sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-hub-vocabulary-source.cjs` fails on the `alias`, `stage-two`, `triggers` and `packets` legs; its `stage-two-reverse` leg only reports.\n59: Stage 2 (mode → leaves) lives in the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md), which maps the request's authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources that mode loads.\n60: The two layers stay separate: the hub never emits leaf paths, and the surface router never re-decides the mode.\n61: The advisor routes every documentation and authoring query to the single identity `sk-doc`.\n62: Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"`.\n63: Act on the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\n64: Compiled routing is the default.\n65: An unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation, because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n66: Run the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n71: \n72: ### Terms\n73: \n74: - **`workflowMode`**: the public packet key a request resolves to, such as `sk-create-skill`.\n75: - **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for every sk-doc packet, because this hub has no surface axis.\n76: - **`backendKind`**: `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators and `sk-create-quality-control` for the quality-control mode.\n77: - **packet**: a nested `sk-create-*` folder that keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets and scripts.\n78: - **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each packet's discriminator, aliases, command and `advisorRouting`.\n79: - **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource and bundle rules.\n80: - **`vocabularyClasses`**: the one authored routing vocabulary that the registry aliases, the `Keyword triggers:` lines and the `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against.\n81: - **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP`, which map an authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources its mode loads.\n82: - **leaf**: a canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair from `leaf-manifest.json` that a `RESOURCE_MAP` path converts to.\n83: - **`defer`**: the outcome that asks for disambiguation, which this hub reaches because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n84: - **shared backbone**: the `shared/` copy of the sk-create-quality-control pipeline that every packet consumes.\n85: - **`graph-metadata.json`**: the one advisor identity for the whole skill, which no packet or `shared/` directory carries.\n86: \n87: ### Layout\n88: ```\n89: sk-doc/\n90:   SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-packet logic)\n91:   ROUTER.md              # stage-two surface router (authoring intent -> leaf sets)\n92:   mode-registry.json     # the fifteen-mode discriminator + advisorRouting (single source of truth)\n93:   hub-router.json        # router signals + vocabulary classes\n94:   description.json       # hub advisor descriptor\n95:   graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n96:   changelog/  manual-testing-playbook/  benchmark/  feature-catalog/\n97:   sk-create-skill/  sk-create-readme/  sk-create-agent/  sk-create-command/\n98:   sk-create-feature-catalog/  sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/\n99:   sk-create-benchmark/  sk-create-changelog/  sk-create-diff/\n100:   sk-create-repo-rule/  sk-create-frontmatter/  sk-create-goal/\n101:   sk-create-with-human-voice/  sk-create-quality-control/    # nested workflow packets\n102:   scripts/               # facade symlinks -> shared/ + owning packets (tool paths only)\n103:   shared/                # sk-create-quality-control backbone: validators, global standards, shared assets\n104: ```\n105: \n106: Each packet is self-contained (its own `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `changelog/`, and moved `references/`/`assets/`/`scripts/`) and carries **no** `graph-metadata.json`, so the advisor discovers exactly one `sk-doc` identity.\n107: \n108: ### Shared backbone\n109: `shared/` holds the universal sk-create-quality-control pipeline consumed by every packet:\n110: - Generic validator scripts in `shared/scripts/`.\n111: - Cross-cutting standards and vocabulary in `shared/references/`.\n112: - Shared templates in `shared/assets/`.\n113: \n114: The generic validator `shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs` counts and resolves the `<path>.<ext>:<line>` citations in every tracked skill doc.\n115: It makes zero model calls by default.\n116: `--jev` runs the backend and needs `--out <dir>`, so every call is recorded, and the Jev arm and the advisory live in the sibling `shared/scripts/classifier-cite-drift-scan.mjs`.\n117: `validate_document.py` runs the same check as a non-blocking advisory on the document it validates.\n118: It prints `cite-drift advisory:` lines only when a Jev credential is stored, never changes the exit code, and `JEV_FEATURE_CITE_DRIFT=0` (older name: `SKDOC_CITE_DRIFT_CHECK=0`) skips it.\n119: The `sk-doc/scripts/` root directory keeps facade symlinks pointing inward to `shared/` and the owning packets so tool paths resolve.\n120: There are no hub-root `assets/` or `references/` aggregation directories: consumers reference each packet's own `assets/`/`references/` or the `shared/` backbone directly.\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 4. RULES\n125: \n126: ### ✅ ALWAYS\n127: - **ALWAYS** resolve a packet through `mode-registry.json`; never hardcode a router mapping in the hub.\n128: - **ALWAYS** keep authoring contracts in the packets; the hub stays routing-only.\n129: - **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one identity.\n130: - **ALWAYS** keep the root `ROUTER.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` in sync with `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` — the leaf sets dual-read to canonical typed pairs at the one contract boundary.\n131: - **ALWAYS** keep the sk-create-quality-control pipeline as one shared source under `shared/`, consumed by the packets.\n132: - **ALWAYS** keep changelogs as real files at the hub and in each packet — never symlinked.\n133: \n134: ### ⛔ NEVER\n135: - **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` inside a packet or `shared/`.\n136: - **NEVER** put per-packet authoring logic in the hub.\n137: - **NEVER** add a surface axis or a `surfaceBundle` outcome — sk-doc is workflow-only.\n138: \n139: ### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n140: - A new documentation workflow is needed — extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet; do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n141: - A packet would become a near-empty shell (generic doctrine, no type-specific behavior) — fold it into `shared/` instead.\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: ## 5. REFERENCES\n146: \n147: - Registry: `mode-registry.json` (fifteen modes across fourteen packets, `packetKind: workflow`).\n148: - Hub router: `hub-router.json` (signals + vocabulary classes).\n149: - Surface router: `ROUTER.md` (authoring intent to packet-local leaf sets).\n150: - Advisor descriptor: `description.json`; skill-graph identity: `graph-metadata.json`.\n151: - Packets: `sk-create-skill/`, `sk-create-readme/`, `sk-create-agent/`, `sk-create-command/`, `sk-create-feature-catalog/`, `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/`, `sk-create-benchmark/`, `sk-create-changelog/`, `sk-create-diff/`, `sk-create-repo-rule/`, `sk-create-frontmatter/`, `sk-create-goal/`, `sk-create-with-human-voice/`, `sk-create-quality-control/`.\n152: - Shared backbone: `shared/scripts/`, `shared/references/`, `shared/assets/`.\n153: - Parent-skill pattern: `sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md, lines 1-153\n1: ---\n2: name: sk-doc\n3: description: \"Documentation & component authoring hub: skills, agents, commands, READMEs, catalogs, playbooks, changelogs, goals, frontmatter.\"\n4: allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n5: version: 2.9.13.0\n6: metadata:\n7:   family: sk-util\n8: ---\n9: \n10: <!-- Keywords: sk-doc, documentation, markdown, authoring, parent-hub, mode-registry, hub-router, workflowmode, packetkind, sk-create-skill, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, sk-create-quality-control, human-voice-rules, hvr, shared-backbone, create-quality-control-pipeline -->\n11: \n12: # Documentation Authoring Hub (sk-doc)\n13: \n14: One advisor identity, fifteen workflow modes across fourteen packets, one shared sk-create-quality-control backbone.\n15: `sk-doc` is the parent hub for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring.\n16: It holds NO per-packet logic: it routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each packet keeps its own contract in its nested folder.\n17: The cross-cutting sk-create-quality-control pipeline (validators, global standards, frontmatter/llms/template assets) lives once in `shared/` and is consumed by every packet.\n18: \n19: **Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`; `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value, so every hub-root JSON routing file states the same release; `ROUTER.md` keeps its own document version.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n24: \n25: Use this skill for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring, and for document-quality work. The hub classifies the request, resolves a `workflowMode`, and loads the matching nested packet.\n26: \n27: | Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command |\n28: |------|------------|--------|---------|\n29: | **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n30: | **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder README, general or code-folder | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n31: | **sk-create-agent** | Scaffold an OpenCode agent (permission/authority frontmatter) | `sk-create-agent/` | `/create:agent` |\n32: | **sk-create-command** | Scaffold an OpenCode slash command (argument-hint + allowed-tools + router/presentation split) | `sk-create-command/` | `/create:command` |\n33: | **sk-create-feature-catalog** | Author a feature-catalog inventory package | `sk-create-feature-catalog/` | `/create:feature-catalog` |\n34: | **sk-create-manual-testing-playbook** | Author a manual-testing-playbook package | `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/` | `/create:manual-testing-playbook` |\n35: | **sk-create-benchmark** | Author MCP-promotion and behavior packages or inputs | `sk-create-benchmark/` | `/create:benchmark` |\n36: | **sk-create-changelog** | Author a global component changelog entry (version bump + topology-aware placement). Packet-local changelogs are deprecated | `sk-create-changelog/` | `/create:changelog` |\n37: | **sk-create-diff** | Produce a local, Git-free before/after review of an edited document (text/Markdown/HTML/DOCX/text-PDF) as a self-contained HTML report | `sk-create-diff/` | `/create:diff` |\n38: | **sk-create-repo-rule** | Create, revise or retire a repo-local rule under `repo-rules/` and wire it into `REPO RULES.md` (four decision tests refuse most requests) | `sk-create-repo-rule/` | `/create:repo-rule` |\n39: | **sk-create-with-human-voice** | Apply the Human Voice Rules to prose, or score prose against them, with a scope gate and a re-scan | `sk-create-with-human-voice/` | `/create:with-human-voice` |\n40: | **sk-create-frontmatter** | Own the YAML frontmatter contract: per-class field rules, the description budget, and the 4-part `version` derivation | `sk-create-frontmatter/` | — (routes via aliases) |\n41: | **sk-create-goal** | Author or revise a packet `goal.md`: the durable directive, three to seven self-contained completion criteria, and the phase-parent binding table (session-goal setting stays with the goal hooks) | `sk-create-goal/` | `/create:goal` |\n42: | **sk-create-quality-control** | Validate / score / optimize an EXISTING document (extract → DQI → HVR → validate) | `sk-create-quality-control/` | (routes via aliases) |\n43: \n44: ### When NOT to Use\n45: - Code implementation, tests, or debugging — use `sk-code`.\n46: - Git worktree, branch, commit, PR, or release work — use `sk-git`.\n47: - Spec-folder workflow / memory / save context — use `system-spec-kit`.\n48: - A measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source) — use `sk-design-md-generator`.\n49: - The `shared/` backbone is consumed by the packets, not invoked as a user workflow.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n54: \n55: Routing is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\n56: Stage 1 (hub → mode) selects a mode: `hub-router.json` `vocabularyClasses` is the one authored routing vocabulary.\n57: The `mode-registry.json` aliases, each packet's `Keyword triggers:` line and the root `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against it.\n58: `sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-hub-vocabulary-source.cjs` fails on the `alias`, `stage-two`, `triggers` and `packets` legs; its `stage-two-reverse` leg only reports.\n59: Stage 2 (mode → leaves) lives in the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md), which maps the request's authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources that mode loads.\n60: The two layers stay separate: the hub never emits leaf paths, and the surface router never re-decides the mode.\n61: The advisor routes every documentation and authoring query to the single identity `sk-doc`.\n62: Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"`.\n63: Act on the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\n64: Compiled routing is the default.\n65: An unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation, because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n66: Run the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n71: \n72: ### Terms\n73: \n74: - **`workflowMode`**: the public packet key a request resolves to, such as `sk-create-skill`.\n75: - **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for every sk-doc packet, because this hub has no surface axis.\n76: - **`backendKind`**: `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators and `sk-create-quality-control` for the quality-control mode.\n77: - **packet**: a nested `sk-create-*` folder that keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets and scripts.\n78: - **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each packet's discriminator, aliases, command and `advisorRouting`.\n79: - **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource and bundle rules.\n80: - **`vocabularyClasses`**: the one authored routing vocabulary that the registry aliases, the `Keyword triggers:` lines and the `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against.\n81: - **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP`, which map an authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources its mode loads.\n82: - **leaf**: a canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair from `leaf-manifest.json` that a `RESOURCE_MAP` path converts to.\n83: - **`defer`**: the outcome that asks for disambiguation, which this hub reaches because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n84: - **shared backbone**: the `shared/` copy of the sk-create-quality-control pipeline that every packet consumes.\n85: - **`graph-metadata.json`**: the one advisor identity for the whole skill, which no packet or `shared/` directory carries.\n86: \n87: ### Layout\n88: ```\n89: sk-doc/\n90:   SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-packet logic)\n91:   ROUTER.md              # stage-two surface router (authoring intent -> leaf sets)\n92:   mode-registry.json     # the fifteen-mode discriminator + advisorRouting (single source of truth)\n93:   hub-router.json        # router signals + vocabulary classes\n94:   description.json       # hub advisor descriptor\n95:   graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n96:   changelog/  manual-testing-playbook/  benchmark/  feature-catalog/\n97:   sk-create-skill/  sk-create-readme/  sk-create-agent/  sk-create-command/\n98:   sk-create-feature-catalog/  sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/\n99:   sk-create-benchmark/  sk-create-changelog/  sk-create-diff/\n100:   sk-create-repo-rule/  sk-create-frontmatter/  sk-create-goal/\n101:   sk-create-with-human-voice/  sk-create-quality-control/    # nested workflow packets\n102:   scripts/               # facade symlinks -> shared/ + owning packets (tool paths only)\n103:   shared/                # sk-create-quality-control backbone: validators, global standards, shared assets\n104: ```\n105: \n106: Each packet is self-contained (its own `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `changelog/`, and moved `references/`/`assets/`/`scripts/`) and carries **no** `graph-metadata.json`, so the advisor discovers exactly one `sk-doc` identity.\n107: \n108: ### Shared backbone\n109: `shared/` holds the universal sk-create-quality-control pipeline consumed by every packet:\n110: - Generic validator scripts in `shared/scripts/`.\n111: - Cross-cutting standards and vocabulary in `shared/references/`.\n112: - Shared templates in `shared/assets/`.\n113: \n114: The generic validator `shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs` counts and resolves the `<path>.<ext>:<line>` citations in every tracked skill doc.\n115: It makes zero model calls by default.\n116: `--jev` runs the backend and needs `--out <dir>`, so every call is recorded, and the Jev arm and the advisory live in the sibling `shared/scripts/classifier-cite-drift-scan.mjs`.\n117: `validate_document.py` runs the same check as a non-blocking advisory on the document it validates.\n118: It prints `cite-drift advisory:` lines only when a Jev credential is stored, never changes the exit code, and `JEV_FEATURE_CITE_DRIFT=0` (older name: `SKDOC_CITE_DRIFT_CHECK=0`) skips it.\n119: The `sk-doc/scripts/` root directory keeps facade symlinks pointing inward to `shared/` and the owning packets so tool paths resolve.\n120: There are no hub-root `assets/` or `references/` aggregation directories: consumers reference each packet's own `assets/`/`references/` or the `shared/` backbone directly.\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 4. RULES\n125: \n126: ### ✅ ALWAYS\n127: - **ALWAYS** resolve a packet through `mode-registry.json`; never hardcode a router mapping in the hub.\n128: - **ALWAYS** keep authoring contracts in the packets; the hub stays routing-only.\n129: - **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one identity.\n130: - **ALWAYS** keep the root `ROUTER.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` in sync with `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` — the leaf sets dual-read to canonical typed pairs at the one contract boundary.\n131: - **ALWAYS** keep the sk-create-quality-control pipeline as one shared source under `shared/`, consumed by the packets.\n132: - **ALWAYS** keep changelogs as real files at the hub and in each packet — never symlinked.\n133: \n134: ### ⛔ NEVER\n135: - **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` inside a packet or `shared/`.\n136: - **NEVER** put per-packet authoring logic in the hub.\n137: - **NEVER** add a surface axis or a `surfaceBundle` outcome — sk-doc is workflow-only.\n138: \n139: ### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n140: - A new documentation workflow is needed — extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet; do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n141: - A packet would become a near-empty shell (generic doctrine, no type-specific behavior) — fold it into `shared/` instead.\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: ## 5. REFERENCES\n146: \n147: - Registry: `mode-registry.json` (fifteen modes across fourteen packets, `packetKind: workflow`).\n148: - Hub router: `hub-router.json` (signals + vocabulary classes).\n149: - Surface router: `ROUTER.md` (authoring intent to packet-local leaf sets).\n150: - Advisor descriptor: `description.json`; skill-graph identity: `graph-metadata.json`.\n151: - Packets: `sk-create-skill/`, `sk-create-readme/`, `sk-create-agent/`, `sk-create-command/`, `sk-create-feature-catalog/`, `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/`, `sk-create-benchmark/`, `sk-create-changelog/`, `sk-create-diff/`, `sk-create-repo-rule/`, `sk-create-frontmatter/`, `sk-create-goal/`, `sk-create-with-human-voice/`, `sk-create-quality-control/`.\n152: - Shared backbone: `shared/scripts/`, `shared/references/`, `shared/assets/`.\n153: - Parent-skill pattern: `sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582798331,"end":1794582799730}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582799766,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffep6y7sQ71Rop5Va","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5785fb2001gB566bWgGOz77L","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffep6y7sQ71Rop5Va","messageID":"msg_1d5783b04001UeOAWgbUX0fEoA","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab78e26d4deeb724","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json, lines 1-526\n1: [\n2:   {\n3:     \"command\": \"/create:skill\",\n4:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-skill\",\n5:     \"description\": \"Create or update OpenCode skills via one unified command with operation routing. :auto/:confirm.\",\n6:     \"argumentHint\": \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n7:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n8:     \"gate3_location\": \"a new or updated OpenCode skill package at --path or the path setup resolves\",\n9:     \"userIntent\": {\n10:       \"job\": \"I want to create or update a standalone OpenCode skill package.\",\n11:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n12:         \"create an OpenCode skill\",\n13:         \"scaffold a skill package\",\n14:         \"update a skill definition\"\n15:       ]\n16:     },\n17:     \"choreography\": [\n18:       {\n19:         \"order\": 1,\n20:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n21:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n22:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n23:       },\n24:       {\n25:         \"order\": 2,\n26:         \"skill\": \"create-skill\",\n27:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md\",\n28:         \"action\": \"load the standalone-skill scaffolding mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n29:       },\n30:       {\n31:         \"order\": 3,\n32:         \"skill\": \"create-skill\",\n33:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt\",\n34:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n35:       }\n36:     ],\n37:     \"discriminator\": {\n38:       \"whenToUse\": \"Use this command when the deliverable is a standalone OpenCode skill or a shared skill packet.\",\n39:       \"preferSiblingWhen\": [\n40:         {\n41:           \"sibling\": \"/create:skill-parent\",\n42:           \"when\": \"Prefer the parent command when the deliverable is a hub with multiple nested workflow or surface packets.\"\n43:         }\n44:       ]\n45:     }\n46:   },\n47:   {\n48:     \"command\": \"/create:skill-parent\",\n49:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-skill-parent\",\n50:     \"description\": \"Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets (one hub identity, registry source of truth). :auto/:confirm.\",\n51:     \"argumentHint\": \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--modes <mode1,mode2,...>] [--surfaces <s1,s2,...>] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n52:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n53:     \"gate3_location\": \"a parent skill hub with nested mode packets, one graph-metadata.json, at the resolved --path\",\n54:     \"userIntent\": {\n55:       \"job\": \"I want to scaffold or update a parent skill hub with nested mode packets.\",\n56:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n57:         \"create a parent skill hub\",\n58:         \"add nested mode packets\",\n59:         \"scaffold a skill router\"\n60:       ]\n61:     },\n62:     \"choreography\": [\n63:       {\n64:         \"order\": 1,\n65:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n66:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n67:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n68:       },\n69:       {\n70:         \"order\": 2,\n71:         \"skill\": \"create-skill\",\n72:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/SKILL.md\",\n73:         \"action\": \"load the parent-hub scaffolding mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n74:       },\n75:       {\n76:         \"order\": 3,\n77:         \"skill\": \"create-skill\",\n78:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-parent-presentation.txt\",\n79:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n80:       }\n81:     ],\n82:     \"discriminator\": {\n83:       \"whenToUse\": \"Use this command when the deliverable is a parent skill hub with nested workflow or surface packets.\",\n84:       \"preferSiblingWhen\": [\n85:         {\n86:           \"sibling\": \"/create:skill\",\n87:           \"when\": \"Prefer the standalone command when the deliverable is one skill package without a multi-packet hub.\"\n88:         }\n89:       ]\n90:     }\n91:   },\n92:   {\n93:     \"command\": \"/create:readme\",\n94:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-readme\",\n95:     \"description\": \"Folder README creation, general or code-folder, with sk-doc quality standards. Modes :auto, :confirm.\",\n96:     \"argumentHint\": \"<target> [--type <project|component|feature|skill>] [--output <path>] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n97:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n98:     \"gate3_location\": \"a README file in the target folder, or at the --output path\",\n99:     \"userIntent\": {\n100:       \"job\": \"I want to write a current-state README for a folder.\",\n101:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n102:         \"write a folder README\",\n103:         \"document a project folder\"\n104:       ]\n105:     },\n106:     \"choreography\": [\n107:       {\n108:         \"order\": 1,\n109:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n110:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n111:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n112:       },\n113:       {\n114:         \"order\": 2,\n115:         \"skill\": \"create-readme\",\n116:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/SKILL.md\",\n117:         \"action\": \"load the README authoring mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n118:       },\n119:       {\n120:         \"order\": 3,\n121:         \"skill\": \"create-readme\",\n122:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-readme-presentation.txt\",\n123:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n124:       }\n125:     ]\n126:   },\n127:   {\n128:     \"command\": \"/create:agent\",\n129:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-agent\",\n130:     \"description\": \"Create a new OpenCode agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, behavioral rules. Modes :auto, :confirm.\",\n131:     \"argumentHint\": \"<agent_name> [agent_description] [:auto|:confirm] (:auto supports PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: prompt-body block for non-interactive setup)\",\n132:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n133:     \"gate3_location\": \"a new agent file under .skilled/agents/ and its runtime mirrors\",\n134:     \"userIntent\": {\n135:       \"job\": \"I want to create an OpenCode agent with explicit permissions and behavioral rules.\",\n136:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n137:         \"create an OpenCode agent\",\n138:         \"define agent permissions\",\n139:         \"write an agent persona\"\n140:       ]\n141:     },\n142:     \"choreography\": [\n143:       {\n144:         \"order\": 1,\n145:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n146:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n147:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n148:       },\n149:       {\n150:         \"order\": 2,\n151:         \"skill\": \"create-agent\",\n152:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-agent/SKILL.md\",\n153:         \"action\": \"load the agent-authoring mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n154:       },\n155:       {\n156:         \"order\": 3,\n157:         \"skill\": \"create-agent\",\n158:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-agent-presentation.txt\",\n159:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n160:       }\n161:     ]\n162:   },\n163:   {\n164:     \"command\": \"/create:command\",\n165:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-command\",\n166:     \"description\": \"Create or update OpenCode slash command sets with :auto/:confirm workflow assets.\",\n167:     \"argumentHint\": \"<command_invocation> [command_request] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n168:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n169:     \"gate3_location\": \"a slash command file plus its auto and confirm workflow YAML assets\",\n170:     \"userIntent\": {\n171:       \"job\": \"I want to create or update an OpenCode slash command with routed workflow assets.\",\n172:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n173:         \"create a slash command\",\n174:         \"scaffold command routing\",\n175:         \"write command frontmatter\"\n176:       ]\n177:     },\n178:     \"choreography\": [\n179:       {\n180:         \"order\": 1,\n181:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n182:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n183:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n184:       },\n185:       {\n186:         \"order\": 2,\n187:         \"skill\": \"create-command\",\n188:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/SKILL.md\",\n189:         \"action\": \"load the slash-command authoring mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n190:       },\n191:       {\n192:         \"order\": 3,\n193:         \"skill\": \"create-command\",\n194:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-command-presentation.txt\",\n195:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n196:       }\n197:     ]\n198:   },\n199:   {\n200:     \"command\": \"/create:feature-catalog\",\n201:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-feature-catalog\",\n202:     \"description\": \"Create or update feature catalog packages via one unified command. Modes :auto, :confirm.\",\n203:     \"argumentHint\": \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n204:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n205:     \"gate3_location\": \"a feature catalog package with per-feature docs at --path or the resolved location\",\n206:     \"userIntent\": {\n207:       \"job\": \"I want to build a feature catalog with auditable per-feature documentation.\",\n208:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n209:         \"build a feature catalog\",\n210:         \"inventory system capabilities\",\n211:         \"add per-feature documentation\"\n212:       ]\n213:     },\n214:     \"choreography\": [\n215:       {\n216:         \"order\": 1,\n217:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n218:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n219:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n220:       },\n221:       {\n222:         \"order\": 2,\n223:         \"skill\": \"create-feature-catalog\",\n224:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-feature-catalog/SKILL.md\",\n225:         \"action\": \"load the feature-catalog authoring mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n226:       },\n227:       {\n228:         \"order\": 3,\n229:         \"skill\": \"create-feature-catalog\",\n230:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-feature-catalog-presentation.txt\",\n231:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n232:       }\n233:     ]\n234:   },\n235:   {\n236:     \"command\": \"/create:manual-testing-playbook\",\n237:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-manual-testing-playbook\",\n238:     \"description\": \"Create or update manual testing playbook packages via one unified command. Modes :auto, :confirm.\",\n239:     \"argumentHint\": \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n240:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n241:     \"gate3_location\": \"a manual testing playbook package with scenario and evidence docs at the resolved --path\",\n242:     \"userIntent\": {\n243:       \"job\": \"I want to author a deterministic manual testing playbook with evidence capture.\",\n244:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n245:         \"create a testing playbook\",\n246:         \"write deterministic test scenarios\",\n247:         \"plan evidence collection\"\n248:       ]\n249:     },\n250:     \"choreography\": [\n251:       {\n252:         \"order\": 1,\n253:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n254:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n255:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n256:       },\n257:       {\n258:         \"order\": 2,\n259:         \"skill\": \"create-manual-testing-playbook\",\n260:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/SKILL.md\",\n261:         \"action\": \"load the manual-testing-playbook authoring mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n262:       },\n263:       {\n264:         \"order\": 3,\n265:         \"skill\": \"create-manual-testing-playbook\",\n266:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-manual-testing-playbook-presentation.txt\",\n267:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n268:       }\n269:     ]\n270:   },\n271:   {\n272:     \"command\": \"/create:benchmark\",\n273:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-benchmark\",\n274:     \"description\": \"Author or update family-keyed benchmark packages. Modes :auto, :confirm.\",\n275:     \"argumentHint\": \"<skill-or-mode> <spec-packet> [create|update] --family=<family> [--benchmark-id <id>] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n276:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n277:     \"gate3_location\": \"family-keyed benchmark artifacts and fixtures at --path or the family's resolved location\",\n278:     \"userIntent\": {\n279:       \"job\": \"I want to author benchmark artifacts, fixtures, or conformance packages for a skill or mode.\",\n280:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n281:         \"author benchmark artifacts\",\n282:         \"create a conformance benchmark\",\n283:         \"write benchmark fixtures\"\n284:       ]\n285:     },\n286:     \"choreography\": [\n287:       {\n288:         \"order\": 1,\n289:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n290:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n291:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n292:       },\n293:       {\n294:         \"order\": 2,\n295:         \"skill\": \"create-benchmark\",\n296:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-benchmark/SKILL.md\",\n297:         \"action\": \"load the benchmark-authoring mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n298:       },\n299:       {\n300:         \"order\": 3,\n301:         \"skill\": \"create-benchmark\",\n302:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-benchmark-presentation.txt\",\n303:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n304:       }\n305:     ]\n306:   },\n307:   {\n308:     \"command\": \"/create:changelog\",\n309:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-changelog\",\n310:     \"description\": \"Create a global changelog entry. Topology-aware, optional GitHub release. :auto/:confirm.\",\n311:     \"argumentHint\": \"<spec-folder-or-component> [--bump <major|minor|patch|build>] [--release] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n312:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n313:     \"gate3_location\": \"a changelog entry under .skilled/changelog/, plus a pushed tag and a published GitHub release when --release is passed\",\n314:     \"ask_first\": [\"outside-repo\"],\n315:     \"userIntent\": {\n316:       \"job\": \"I want to create a global component changelog with release notes.\",\n317:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n318:         \"write release notes\",\n319:         \"create a packet changelog\",\n320:         \"bump a component version\"\n321:       ]\n322:     },\n323:     \"choreography\": [\n324:       {\n325:         \"order\": 1,\n326:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n327:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n328:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n329:       },\n330:       {\n331:         \"order\": 2,\n332:         \"skill\": \"create-changelog\",\n333:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-changelog/SKILL.md\",\n334:         \"action\": \"load the changelog authoring mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n335:       },\n336:       {\n337:         \"order\": 3,\n338:         \"skill\": \"create-changelog\",\n339:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-changelog-presentation.txt\",\n340:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n341:       }\n342:     ]\n343:   },\n344:   {\n345:     \"command\": \"/create:diff\",\n346:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-diff\",\n347:     \"description\": \"Create a self-contained before/after document diff report via the create-diff engine. Modes :auto, :confirm.\",\n348:     \"argumentHint\": \"<target-document | --before old --after new> [--report out.html] [--view unified|side-by-side] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n349:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n350:     \"gate3_location\": \"a self-contained HTML diff report at the --report path the user names\",\n351:     \"userIntent\": {\n352:       \"job\": \"I want to compare document versions and produce a self-contained HTML diff report.\",\n353:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n354:         \"compare document versions\",\n355:         \"review a document diff\",\n356:         \"make an HTML diff report\"\n357:       ]\n358:     },\n359:     \"choreography\": [\n360:       {\n361:         \"order\": 1,\n362:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n363:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n364:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n365:       },\n366:       {\n367:         \"order\": 2,\n368:         \"skill\": \"create-diff\",\n369:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-diff/SKILL.md\",\n370:         \"action\": \"load the document-diff mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n371:       },\n372:       {\n373:         \"order\": 3,\n374:         \"skill\": \"create-diff\",\n375:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-diff-presentation.txt\",\n376:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n377:       }\n378:     ]\n379:   },\n380:   {\n381:     \"command\": \"/create:repo-rule\",\n382:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-repo-rule\",\n383:     \"description\": \"Create, revise or retire a repo rule under repo-rules/, wired into REPO RULES.md. :auto/:confirm.\",\n384:     \"argumentHint\": \"<what the rule should bind> [create|revise|retire] [--rule <name>] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n385:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n386:     \"gate3_location\": \"a rule file under repo-rules/, wired into that repository's REPO RULES.md\",\n387:     \"userIntent\": {\n388:       \"job\": \"I want a repo-local rule that binds before an action, or I want to change or remove one.\",\n389:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n390:         \"create a repo rule\",\n391:         \"add a project rule\",\n392:         \"retire a repo rule\",\n393:         \"wire a rule into REPO RULES.md\"\n394:       ]\n395:     },\n396:     \"choreography\": [\n397:       {\n398:         \"order\": 1,\n399:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n400:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n401:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n402:       },\n403:       {\n404:         \"order\": 2,\n405:         \"skill\": \"create-repo-rule\",\n406:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-repo-rule/SKILL.md\",\n407:         \"action\": \"load the repo-rule authoring mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n408:       },\n409:       {\n410:         \"order\": 3,\n411:         \"skill\": \"create-repo-rule\",\n412:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-repo-rule-presentation.txt\",\n413:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n414:       }\n415:     ],\n416:     \"discriminator\": {\n417:       \"whenToUse\": \"Use this command when the deliverable constrains what may be done before an action \\u2014 a rule loaded by a trigger table.\",\n418:       \"preferSiblingWhen\": [\n419:         {\n420:           \"sibling\": \"/create:skill\",\n421:           \"when\": \"Prefer the skill command when the deliverable teaches how to accomplish something rather than constraining how it is done.\"\n422:         },\n423:         {\n424:           \"sibling\": \"/create:command\",\n425:           \"when\": \"Prefer the command command when the deliverable is a slash command rather than a rule.\"\n426:         }\n427:       ]\n428:     }\n429:   },\n430:   {\n431:     \"command\": \"/create:with-human-voice\",\n432:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-with-human-voice\",\n433:     \"description\": \"Apply or score prose against the Human Voice Rules with a scope gate and a re-scan. :auto/:confirm.\",\n434:     \"argumentHint\": \"<file or passage> [apply|score] [--include-code] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n435:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n436:     \"gate3_location\": \"the target file rewritten in place by apply; score writes no file\",\n437:     \"userIntent\": {\n438:       \"job\": \"I want prose brought up to the Human Voice Rules, or told how far off it is.\",\n439:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n440:         \"make this sound human\",\n441:         \"it reads like AI wrote it\",\n442:         \"apply the human voice rules\",\n443:         \"score this against HVR\"\n444:       ]\n445:     },\n446:     \"choreography\": [\n447:       {\n448:         \"order\": 1,\n449:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n450:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n451:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n452:       },\n453:       {\n454:         \"order\": 2,\n455:         \"skill\": \"create-with-human-voice\",\n456:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-with-human-voice/SKILL.md\",\n457:         \"action\": \"load the voice-application mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n458:       },\n459:       {\n460:         \"order\": 3,\n461:         \"skill\": \"create-with-human-voice\",\n462:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-with-human-voice-presentation.txt\",\n463:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n464:       }\n465:     ],\n466:     \"discriminator\": {\n467:       \"whenToUse\": \"Use this command when the deliverable is prose that has to read as a person wrote it, and the target already exists.\",\n468:       \"preferSiblingWhen\": [\n469:         {\n470:           \"sibling\": \"sk-create-quality-control\",\n471:           \"when\": \"Prefer the document audit mode, which the hub reaches by routing rather than by a command, when the target needs structure, DQI and validator results rather than a voice pass.\"\n472:         },\n473:         {\n474:           \"sibling\": \"/create:readme\",\n475:           \"when\": \"Prefer the README command when the document does not exist yet. Author it first, then run the voice pass over what came out.\"\n476:         }\n477:       ]\n478:     }\n479:   },\n480:   {\n481:     \"command\": \"/create:goal\",\n482:     \"ownerMode\": \"sk-create-goal\",\n483:     \"description\": \"Author or revise a packet goal.md: top-level, phase-parent, child, retrofit, phase-add, amend. :auto/:confirm.\",\n484:     \"argumentHint\": \"<packet path> [top-level|phase-parent|child|retrofit|phase-add|amend] [:auto|:confirm]\",\n485:     \"mutating\": \"mutates\",\n486:     \"gate3_location\": \"a goal.md inside the spec packet the user names\",\n487:     \"userIntent\": {\n488:       \"job\": \"I want a spec packet's goal.md authored, added or revised from that packet's own sources.\",\n489:       \"ownedSignals\": [\n490:         \"write a goal.md for a packet\",\n491:         \"author a phase parent goal\",\n492:         \"add a goal to a packet\",\n493:         \"author a nested child goal\"\n494:       ]\n495:     },\n496:     \"choreography\": [\n497:       {\n498:         \"order\": 1,\n499:         \"skill\": \"sk-doc\",\n500:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\n501:         \"action\": \"load the sk-doc parent hub routing table\"\n502:       },\n503:       {\n504:         \"order\": 2,\n505:         \"skill\": \"create-goal\",\n506:         \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-goal/SKILL.md\",\n507:         \"action\": \"load the packet-goal authoring mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n508:       },\n509:       {\n510:         \"order\": 3,\n511:         \"skill\": \"create-goal\",\n512:         \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/create/assets/create-goal-presentation.txt\",\n513:         \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n514:       }\n515:     ],\n516:     \"discriminator\": {\n517:       \"whenToUse\": \"Use this command when the deliverable is a spec packet's goal.md (top-level, phase parent or nested child) authored or revised from that packet's own sources.\",\n518:       \"preferSiblingWhen\": [\n519:         {\n520:           \"sibling\": \"/goal-opencode\",\n521:           \"when\": \"Prefer the goal hooks (/goal, /goal-opencode, /goal-pi, /goal-cursor) or the host's native goal command when the request is to set, bind or resend a session objective; thi